{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-72479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,4]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,7]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}5Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}5Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[2,4]$ and $[3,7]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =4-2=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =7-3=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=5\\cdot 2\\cdot 4=40.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-72479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "20"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "55"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "40"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,1]$ and $[1,2]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =1-0=1, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =2-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have \n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-72476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-72476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,8]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[2,3]$ and $[3,8]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-2=1, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =8-3=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 1\\cdot 5=20.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-149628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[4,8]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,3]$ and $[4,8]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-0=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =8-4=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=3\\cdot 4=12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-123069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-122867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,2]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,6]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-122867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,2]$ and $[1,6]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-0=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =6-1=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 5=10.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-122867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-122867" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-122867" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-122867" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1,1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1,1]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}10({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n10{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[-1,1].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=1-(-1) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}\\,+\\,{y}_{0})({y}_{1}\\,-\\,{y}_{0})\\,+\\,({y}_{2}\\,+\\,{y}_{1})({y}_{2}\\,-\\,{y}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({y}_{n}\\,+\\,{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}\\,-\\,{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2}-(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n10{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.=10\\cdot 2\\cdot 0=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-123104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-20"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "40"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-123104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,5]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1,2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[3,5].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5-3=2.\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-149631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "48"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,7]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-3,-2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,7].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=7-2 & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}\\,+\\,{y}_{0})({y}_{1}\\,-\\,{y}_{0})\\,+\\,({y}_{2}\\,+\\,{y}_{1})({y}_{2}\\,-\\,{y}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({y}_{n}\\,+\\,{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}\\,-\\,{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-5)=-100.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-149634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-100"] ["math" "-25"] ["math" "-50"] ["math" "100"] ["math" "50"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149634" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-100"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,6]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[4,6]$\n\nCalculate  ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-4=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=32\\cdot 2=64.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-149629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "18"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "64"] ["math" "96"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "64"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-4,-1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[8,9]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-3({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[8,9].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=9-8 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})\\,+\\,({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-(-4)^{2} \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=(-3)\\cdot (-15)\\cdot 1=45.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ab138019ca6150a05dbed04cc22491b5264d2e978f8b2decb0dab66d35e7d10"} {"question" "q-149635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-45"] ["math" "-54"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "45"] ["math" "54"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "q-149635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "45"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/state.json" "file_sha256" "ceb88a2a4efbe20d982e8b7e850dde660ba85d26855dfe470b1123dc0b77fe17"} {"question" "e-9482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1, 2]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 3]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n {3} \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/example-9482.json" "file_sha256" "407921fc7eb72148977a3c1c799d7f5fb41d5adcbc097476b19ccf8d1d31df1c"} {"question" "e-9482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i$ and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[-1, 2]$ and $[2,3]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-(-1)=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =3-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/example-9482.json" "file_sha256" "407921fc7eb72148977a3c1c799d7f5fb41d5adcbc097476b19ccf8d1d31df1c"} {"question" "e-6117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[4, 6]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 6]$\n\nCalculate  $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/example-6117.json" "file_sha256" "4015c44708ce65611be7f3b5eac96f498be5fd4a7e6448e53afdcd22afbe3b23"} {"question" "e-6117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[2, 6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})+({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j = 20\\cdot 4 = 80.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073065/example-6117.json" "file_sha256" "4015c44708ce65611be7f3b5eac96f498be5fd4a7e6448e53afdcd22afbe3b23"}] "usage" {"q-122867" [] "e-6117" [] "e-9482" []} "basis" 2668 "retractions" [[17592186179910 :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0, 2]$\n- $P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[1, 6]$\n\nCalculate $∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δx_{i}Δy_{j}$, where $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$."] [17592186179514 :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1, 2]$\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 3]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n {3} \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j$, where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}$."] [17592186179514 :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)3Δx_{i}Δy_{j} &= 3∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δx_{i}Δy_{j} \\\\\n&= 3∑_(i = 1)^(m)Δx_{i}∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nare just the lengths of the intervals $[-1, 2]$ and $[2,3]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)Δx_{i} &= 2 - (-1) = 3, \\\\\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j} &= 3 - 2 = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 9\n$$"] [17592186179451 :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[4, 6]$\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 6]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j$, where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}$."] [17592186179451 :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nis just the length of the interval $[2, 6]$. So, we have\n\n$$\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j} = 6 - 2 = 4\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i$, we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i} &= (x_{1} + x_{0})Δx_{1} + (x_{2} + x_{1})Δx_{2} + ⋯ + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})Δx_{n} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{0})(x_{1} - x_{0}) + (x_{2} + x_{1})(x_{2} - x_{1}) + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})(x_{m} - x_{m - 1}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&=-x_{0}^{2} + x_{m}^{2} \\\\\n&= x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 6^{2} - 4^{2} \\\\\n&= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j = 20\\cdot 4 = 80\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186177461 17592186177462 17592186177463 17592186177464 17592186177465] "immutable_fields" [[17592186177460 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177460 :answer-field/id] [17592186177460 :answer-field/key] [17592186177460 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
